+# FX P&L Report DAG - Quick Reference
+
+## What Changed?
+
+The `fx_pnl_report` DAG has been updated to better serve the treasury desk's needs:
+
+### Old Behavior
+- ❌ Ran at midnight UTC every day (including weekends)
+- ❌ Reported on the same day as execution
+- ✅ Report filename: `fx_pnl_<execution-date>.csv`
+
+### New Behavior
+- ✅ Runs at **6:00 AM New York time, Monday–Friday only**
+- ✅ **Reports the previous business day**
+- ✅ Report filename: `fx_pnl_<trade-date>.csv` (unchanged format)
+
+## Daily Execution Schedule
+
+| Day | Execution Time | Reports |
+|-----|---|---|
+| **Monday** | 6:00 AM EST | Friday's trades |
+| **Tuesday** | 6:00 AM EST | Monday's trades |
+| **Wednesday** | 6:00 AM EST | Tuesday's trades |
+| **Thursday** | 6:00 AM EST | Wednesday's trades |
+| **Friday** | 6:00 AM EST | Thursday's trades |
+| Saturday | _(no run)_ | — |
+| Sunday | _(no run)_ | — |
+
+## Example File Outputs
+
+```
+Friday morning (Mon 6am):    fx_pnl_2026-02-20.csv
+Monday morning (Tue 6am):    fx_pnl_2026-02-23.csv
+Tuesday morning (Wed 6am):   fx_pnl_2026-02-24.csv
+Wednesday morning (Thu 6am): fx_pnl_2026-02-25.csv
+Thursday morning (Fri 6am):  fx_pnl_2026-02-26.csv
+```
+
+## Excel Integration
+
+**Good news:** No changes needed to your Excel imports!
+
+- ✅ Filename format unchanged: `fx_pnl_YYYY-MM-DD.csv`
+- ✅ Column structure unchanged: `[desk, trades, notional_usd, pnl_usd]`
+- ✅ Column order unchanged
+- ✅ Data format unchanged
+
+Your existing power queries and data imports will continue to work as-is.
+
+## Timezone Handling
+
+The DAG automatically handles daylight saving time transitions. At 6:00 AM New York time:
+- **Winter (EST, UTC-5)**: Runs at 11:00 AM UTC
+- **Summer (EDT, UTC-4)**: Runs at 10:00 AM UTC
+
+The timezone conversion is handled transparently by Airflow.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### "Why didn't I get a Saturday report?"
+The DAG only runs Monday–Friday, so there are no weekend reports. If you need Friday's data, it's available Monday morning at 6:00 AM.
+
+### "Why is today's date not in the report?"
+The DAG reports on the *previous* business day, not the current day. This gives traders time to book closing trades before the overnight report.
+
+### "The report date is from last week—is that right?"
+Yes, if it's Monday morning and you're seeing Friday's date, that's correct. This is the previous business day.
+
+## Questions?
+
+Contact the data engineering team or review the DAG source code in `dags/fx_pnl_report.py`.
